From: beyond2lte camera enablement <noreply@localhost>
Date: 2026-11-23
Subject: [PATCH] pipeline: simple: match the exynos9820-csis media device with SoftISP

The beyond2lte (Exynos 9820, SM-G975F) out-of-tree CSI receiver driver
`exynos9820-csis` does raw Bayer capture with no hardware ISP: the sensor
subdev links straight to a V4L2 video node that DMAs unpacked 10-bit Bayer
(V4L2_PIX_FMT_SGRBG10) into memory. That is exactly the shape the simple
pipeline handler drives with the CPU software ISP (debayer + AGC/AWB/BLC).

The simple pipeline handler only acquires media devices whose driver name is
in `supportedDevices[]`, so the receiver has to be whitelisted here. No
converter hardware exists, so an empty converter list and swIspAllowed=true
select the software ISP path.

Tested against libcamera v0.8.0 (pmaports temp/libcamera fork).

Signed-off-by: beyond2lte camera enablement <noreply@localhost>
---
 src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -258,6 +258,7 @@
 
 static const SimplePipelineInfo supportedDevices[] = {
 	{ "dcmipp", {}, false },
+	{ "exynos9820-csis", {}, true },
 	{ "imx7-csi", { { "pxp", 1 } }, true },
 	{ "intel-ipu6", {}, true },
 	{ "intel-ipu7", {}, true },
